     or to be forced to terminate the retry at the end of the task (in this case, the system takes the last execution result or exception as the final state).
 
   - **AsyncRetryPredicate**: The retry condition can be triggered based on the return result or the execution exception.
+    Both `result_predicate` and `exception_predicate` are abstract methods, so a subclass of `AsyncRetryPredicate` must implement them; likewise, subclasses of `AsyncRetryStrategy` must implement `can_retry`, `get_backoff_time_millis` and `get_retry_predicate`. Instantiating an incomplete subclass raises `TypeError`.
+
+  - **Built-in predicates**: The Python API provides three ready-to-use predicate functions in `pyflink.datastream.async_retry_predicates`:
+    - `empty_result_predicate(result)`: returns `True` when the result is `None` or an empty list.
+    - `has_exception_predicate(error)`: returns `True` when an error is present (i.e. not `None`).
+    - `exception_type_predicate(error, expected_error_type)`: returns `True` when the error is an instance of `expected_error_type`.
 
 
